  "preconditions": [
    "Owned current-schema records and read-only model APIs; synthetic actors and hashes are not actual approvals or external test evidence."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Load supported stored records, reject malformed local fields and compare original bytes without executing referenced operations.",
    "Resolve every declared slot for an explicit subject/contract verified_by pair; bind actual contract/test bytes and inspect passive metadata without executing code. Prepare only new draft defaults when no additional dimension is declared.",
    "Resolve direct verified_by tests into implicit overall contracts bound to original Test records. Preserve explicit-contract results and reject incomplete contracts, invalid identities and changed source bindings without file access or test execution.",
    "Derive required keys independently from every applicable subject in an owned whole-project model, native verified_by targets and all slots. Compare descriptor coverage without changing the scope; retain missing or unresolved obligations and reject foreign keys. Bind explicit selected configuration and preserve input files without executing tests or Evidence.",
    "Rebuild native seeds, query pages and closure from a separately supplied ScopeDescriptor and explicit ClosureBindings matched to the whole model inventory. Verify that descriptor selections cannot replace subjects, drop strong dependencies or enlarge scope; report all missing and foreign keys separately."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "Ein Verification-Artefakt MUSS Vorbedingungen, Prüfgegenstand, Verfahren, Oracle oder Pass-Kriterium, erforderliche Evidence-Arten, vollständige `evidence_slots` nach Kapitel 10.5.2 und eine Konfigurationspolicy `independent` oder `bound` definieren.",
    "scope": "Passive record-field contracts and lexical reference constraints only. No graph closure, payload hash verification, document rendering, successful verification or write authorization. Explicit-contract pair resolution and new-draft default are covered; supplied bytes do not prove live inventory or configuration applicability. Direct Test targets now contribute the normative implicit overall check with contract_id=test_id. Neither an invented Verification record nor a configuration-policy guess is produced. 12.l.W adds independent whole-supplied-project obligations for Requirements, Capabilities and Tasks, every explicit slot and direct Test contract. Unknown applicability remains incomplete, excluded required dependencies fail with SRV141, missing keys are incomplete/SRV176 and extra keys SRV175/code 3. Exact coverage is only ready, never passed or proof of live inventory. 12.l.R binds independent native scopes and complete provider inventory; native closure includes required dependencies before comparison. Query pages are recomputed without a verification evaluation. Missing-only keys stay incomplete; foreign keys produce SRV175 with both missing_checks and unexpected_keys and the independently bound required_set_sha256."
  },
